  <part id="P1">
  <!-- Right hand (staff 1): a four-note melody, E5-F5-G5-A5 (pitch classes 4,5,7,9). Left hand (staff 2): a
       steady quarter-note accompaniment under it, Bb2-Bb2-D2-D2 (pitch classes 10,2), chosen to share no pitch
       class with the right hand so pass 2 can never legitimately claim a left-hand key for a right-hand note.
       Grading the right hand alone, every left-hand key becomes a PlayedAlongPress, source "ungraded" - never
       wrong, never extra (FR-024, T092/T093). -->
